tools.description:
Call signature: { tags?: string }

Browse available trigger types. Triggers start workflow execution — schedules (cron),
webhooks, blockchain events, manual triggers, etc. Filter by tags.

Call signature: { type: string }

Get full details of a specific trigger type, including its payload schema.
Use the 'type' field from b3os_list_triggers (e.g. "cronjob", "webhook").

Call signature: { workflowId: string }

Get a workflow's full details including its definition (nodes, triggers, connections).
Use this to inspect an existing workflow before modifying it.

Call signature: { workflowId: string, confirm: true }

Delete (archive) a workflow. This is irreversible. The workflow will be archived
and no longer execute. Always confirm with the user before calling this tool.

Call signature: { workflowId: string }

Pause an active workflow. Its triggers will stop firing and no new runs will start.
Use b3os_resume_workflow to reactivate it.

Call signature: { workflowId: string, limit?: number, offset?: number }

List version history for a workflow. Each publish creates a new version.
Use this to see the change history and find a version to rollback to.

Call signature: { workflowId: string }

Get the schedule information for a workflow — when it last ran and when it will
run next. Only meaningful for workflows with schedule-based triggers (cron).

Call signature: { workflowId?: string, status?: "running"|"success"|"failure"|"waiting"|"cancelled", limit?: number, offset?: number }

List workflow runs. Filter by workflowId and/or status.
Use status="failure" to find failed runs for debugging.

Call signature: { runId: string }

Retry a failed workflow run from the point of failure. Only works on runs with status "failure" or "cancelled". Previously successful nodes are skipped — only failed and pending nodes re-execute.

Use b3os_get_run to inspect the failure first, then retry after fixing the root cause (e.g. updating the workflow definition, fixing connector config).

Call signature: { category?: string, limit?: number, offset?: number }

Browse workflow templates — pre-built workflows that can be cloned or used as
inspiration. Filter by category.

Call signature: { templateId: string }

Get full details of a workflow template including its definition. Use this to
inspect a template before cloning it into a new workflow.
